/*
:name: mem_whole_cond_const
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: mem_whole_cond_const.condconst
:pyrope_top: condconst
*/

// CONDITIONAL whole-array CONST stores to a REGISTERED array: a clear-all arm
// (`arr = 0`) and a fill-all arm (`arr = 0x3f`) each bulk-write every entry,
// coexisting with a per-entry write (`arr[waddr] = wdata`). The two whole-array
// const stores accumulate into one clocked `update` bus via a priority mux (the
// later `fill` arm wins where its path-cond holds), gated by `clr | fill`; the
// per-entry write is exclusive with both. The read comes first and sees the
// committed contents. This is the XiangShan
// `validArray <= '{0,..}` (reset/flush) + per-set write idiom: a const/tuple-lit
// whole-array store to a reg memory (lower_mem_init_store -> lower_mem_update_store).
//
// SIZED 4x6, not 8x10 (2026-08-15). Every idiom above needs only that a
// broadcast store, a decoded per-entry store and a dynamic read coexist -- the
// entry count and data width are free parameters, and `prp-v2prp2v-*` pays for
// them quadratically: its lgcheck oracle falls through to the bounded miter
// (`sat -seq 1..5` over the unrolled array), where 80 flops cost 39s and 24
// cost 7.7s. Widths stay non-power-of-2 (u6/u2, fill = all-ones 0x3f) so the
// width-inference and sign-conversion coverage the odd u10/u3 gave is kept.
pub mod condconst(clr:Bool, fill:Bool, we:Bool, waddr:U2, wdata:U6, idx:U2) -> (r:U6@[0]) {
  reg arr:[4]U6 = nil
  r = arr[idx]
  if clr {
    arr = 0
  } elif fill {
    arr = 0x3f
  } elif we {
    arr[waddr] = wdata
  }
}
